{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inducedSubgraphView(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spanningSubgraphView(edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraphView(vertices:edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph_view"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsSubgraph"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SubDigraph"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"filtered_graph"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GraphOperations"}],"title":"SubgraphView","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView.swift#L34","fileName":"SubgraphView.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:15GraphOperations12SubgraphViewV"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphAdaptor","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" are the kept vertices in the base’s order, at view indices "},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"view keeps two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and renumbered with one array load per entry and no hashing. A spanning subgraph keeps every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex at its base index."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are, and, if an edge set was given,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when it is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices: an edge’s index is its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rank among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a count per 64-bit word, so the rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices: building"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its edge mask would cost O(m). One on every vertex keeps the base’s rows, edge indices and flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The view holds a copy of the base (value semantics), so mutating the original never shows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through. Phase 1 needs a base with vertex indices; a "},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with vertex holes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"traps at construction."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As a "},{"code":"GraphAdaptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", its generation is the base’s, and it reads the base’s attached maps."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"[map, of: vertex]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"[map, ofEdgeAt: position]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" trap for a vertex or an edge the view drops,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and their "},{"code":"checked:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" forms throw. "},{"code":"values(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the base’s, by the base’s positions; an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithm on the view reads it only at the kept edges."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":[